message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "When the 547/727 prime race first misses an 18H deadline"
abstract: "The sharp simultaneous factor stays 17.493385009687... from height one through exp(40.0507)/(2 sqrt(2)) without assuming GRH. If every zero of the eight specified odd primitive Dirichlet L-functions with absolute ordinate greater than 8,590 and at most five million lies on the critical line, the first missed 18H deadline is a loss at a transcendental start between 8.75 and 9.14 times 10^16. Under the same hypothesis, every factor above the sharp height-one factor and at most 2 exp(2.1973) has the same first miss. The factor 19.95 works unconditionally through exp(41.33)/(2 sqrt(2)). The finite zero condition determines every failing start above the height-one optimum on that larger range and gives 6,892,908,140,538 consecutive failing integer starts."
